B. ROE CROSS-CHECK (return_on_equity_pct vs companies.roe_percentage) & EXTREME DIVERGENCES (>10x):
- Target: 91 companies with computed FY24 ROE.
- Confirmation of TCS Anomaly:
  * Computed ROE: 50.9443% (Net Profit Rs 46,099 Cr / Net Worth Rs 90,489 Cr)
  * Source companies.roe_percentage: 0.52% (Divergence: 98.0x multiplier, diff +50.42%)
  * Verdict: CONFIRMED. Source column exhibits an overt 100x decimal/units error (0.52% instead of ~52%).
- Additional Extreme Divergences (>10x Multiplier):
  * BEL: Computed ROE 4744.05% vs Source 26.30% (Multiplier: 180.4x)
    Cause: Raw source balance sheet equity+reserves is Rs 84 Cr vs P&L Net Profit Rs 3,985 Cr.
  * HAL: Computed ROE 3816.58% vs Source 28.90% (Multiplier: 132.1x)
    Cause: Raw source balance sheet equity+reserves is Rs 199 Cr vs P&L Net Profit Rs 7,595 Cr.
- Total Extreme Anomalies (>10x Multiplier): Exactly 3 companies (BEL, HAL, TCS).

